The AmigaOS 3 theme's window decorator and control look, in the style of the
Amiga's Workbench 3.x, made from two public domain themes:

- art/xfwm4: the "Amiga3.x" window decorations for Xfce's xfwm4 by lordwolfchild
  (https://github.com/lordwolfchild/amigaos_xfwm4_themes), released into the public
  domain (LICENSE, the Unlicense). The decorator draws its frame and gadgets from
  these pixels, as its themerc lays them out.
- art/gtk-2.0: the "Amiga3.x" GTK 2 theme by untouchable89 (xfce-look.org, item
  1078934, 2010), which is in the public domain too. The control look draws its
  buttons, check boxes, radio buttons, fields, menus, scroll bars, sliders,
  progress bars and tabs from these pictures, stretched as its .rc files say.

tools/make-amigaos3-art.py turns the pictures into decorator/AmigaOS3WindowArt.h
and controllook/AmigaOS3ControlArt.h. The add-ons' own code is under the MIT
licence, like the rest of Power Theme.
